1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Chime

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:59,980
We'll be right back.

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,300
There, that should do it.

4
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:11,220
I love when you cook for your father and I on Saturdays so I can relax.

5
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:14,120
Yum! Delicious!

6
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:21,320
Unfortunately, my first experience of going to eat ramen with friends turned out to be a dud.

7
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:25,200
Crap, I forgot! But I was so ready to eat some ramen!

8
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:28,960
Naturally, Yoshida was the most disappointed out of all three of us.

9
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:32,640
Low-sodium ramen is garbage! Like, get out of here with that stuff!

10
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,440
We went and got tea instead.

11
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:37,320
Yano and I listened as Yoshida talked about ramen.

12
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:38,800
It was so fun!

13
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:42,360
My friends are so cool!

14
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:44,660
Oh, you're making curry today, Sawako?

15
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:45,900
Huh?

16
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:49,820
Uh, so today's curry, huh?

17
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,520
I'll answer it.

18
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:54,640
Yes, this is Kuro-Numa.

19
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:56,820
Guess I'm being ignored.

20
00:01:58,500 --> 00:01:59,760
It's for Sawako!

21
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:02,300
It's somebody saying they're a friend of yours!

22
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:10,560
Hey, Sawako! Get ready, cause ramen's on the menu tonight!

23
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:11,900
Ramen's on the menu?

24
00:02:12,220 --> 00:02:14,460
Hmph! So, let's get our revenge!

25
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:24,420
My friends are inviting me to get ramen! Can I please go?

26
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:25,600
Friends of yours?

27
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:28,740
Of course you can! Now hurry and go meet with them!

28
00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:30,920
But I haven't started serving the curry yet!

29
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:33,420
Oh, don't you worry! I'll take care of it!

30
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:35,600
Make sure you bring them over sometime, Sawako!

31
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:36,500
Okay!

32
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:40,300
Our little girl is going out with friends!

33
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:44,000
She did mention that she's been having fun lately.

34
00:02:44,340 --> 00:02:48,200
That reminds me about the other day when she came home later than she usually does.

35
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:51,040
Now wait a minute! Are these friends boys or girls?

36
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:52,100
No idea!

37
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:04,540
Oh! You're here!

38
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:09,060
Today I finally get to eat ramen with my friends!

39
00:03:09,060 --> 00:03:14,320
By the way, Sawako, I don't think either of us ever asked you for your cell phone number.

40
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:15,460
What is it?

41
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:17,180
I don't have one.

42
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:18,420
Wait, is that true?

43
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:22,880
Yeah. I've just never felt the need to bother with one, I guess.

44
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:25,080
Ah, that makes sense.

45
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:28,860
Well, if you ever get the urge to buy one, then let us know.

46
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:31,480
Welcome!

47
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:33,620
Come on in, Jizu!

48
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:35,580
You brought some friends with you today?

49
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:37,840
Heck yeah! Now hook us up, Pops!

50
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:41,440
Heh heh heh heh! Can't say no to a request from you, miso!

51
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:43,940
I wanted you to try this ramen no matter what it took!

52
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:45,020
It's the best!

53
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:46,560
I'll just take the usual!

54
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:47,760
You got it!

55
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:50,300
What are you getting? I recommend some miso!

56
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:51,940
Oh, I'll get that then.

57
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:53,820
I'll take a shoyu, please.

58
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:56,260
Was my recommendation not good enough?

59
00:03:56,260 --> 00:03:57,600
I've had it before.

60
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,640
Look! There's no water in here!

61
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:04,460
I'm sorry for the wait.

62
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:07,860
Change it before someone notices!

63
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:08,640
My dad.

64
00:04:08,740 --> 00:04:10,580
I thought I saw Sanada just now.

65
00:04:11,020 --> 00:04:12,420
No, you're right. It's him.

66
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:14,560
Uh-huh. He lives right upstairs from here.

67
00:04:14,820 --> 00:04:15,260
Really?

68
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:18,220
Okay. Miso ramen for you.

69
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:23,220
Looks awesome, right?

70
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:25,140
Thanks a lot for the meal!

71
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:28,880
Man, I'm stuffed.

72
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:31,400
Pops really does make the best ramen in town.

73
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:32,500
Yes, thanks.

74
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:35,340
And it was twice as delicious because I ate it with the two of you.

75
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:37,260
Thanks. We're gonna head upstairs now.

76
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:39,460
Sure. Make yourselves comfortable.

77
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:40,440
Wait, what?

78
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:42,360
Come on in, guys.

79
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:44,460
Interesting. Did you move in here?

80
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:45,780
Huh? No? Why?

81
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:49,020
So, um, can I come along too?

82
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:50,500
Yeah, of course you can.

83
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:51,900
You're real silly, you know that?

84
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:57,380
I've never noticed it before,

85
00:04:57,620 --> 00:04:59,820
but Yoshida and Sanada must be close.

86
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:01,840
Get comfy. There's plenty of room in here.

87
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:04,760
Sorry. Give me a second.

88
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:08,240
Oh, hello.

89
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:10,080
Uh-huh.

90
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:11,300
So popular.

91
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:12,400
What, right now?

92
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:12,960
Huh?

93
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:16,140
Uh, sorry, but I'm hanging out with friends today,

94
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:17,300
so I can't go with you.

95
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:19,040
Huh?

96
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:20,360
They're both girls.

97
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:21,920
Go on, say something.

98
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:24,240
M-Miso ramen is so-

99
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,460
You see?

100
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:28,900
Yeah, okay. I'll message you when I'm done.

101
00:05:29,420 --> 00:05:29,700
Later.

102
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:31,460
Boyfriend?

103
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:33,820
Uh, yeah, it was.

104
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:35,280
She has one?

105
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:37,480
Isn't your current guy in university?

106
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:39,040
You don't need to say current.

107
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:41,940
Wow, you're so grown up, Yano.

108
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:43,980
Ugh, don't you worry.

109
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:46,780
You'll reach the magnificent world of being a grown up too,

110
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:48,440
and it'll happen before you know it.

111
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:50,060
You really think so?

112
00:05:50,540 --> 00:05:52,000
Chizu, same goes for you.

113
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,840
Ugh, you're always saying grown up this, grown up that,

114
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:57,040
but can you defeat 99 dudes in a row?

115
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:57,620
Right.

116
00:05:57,800 --> 00:06:00,800
That weird record you keep of your consecutive wins in middle school.

117
00:06:01,140 --> 00:06:01,480
Weird?

118
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:03,580
What the heck do you even know, you uncultured idiot?

119
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:05,880
I've kind of been wondering why it's only 99.

120
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:07,560
Who was your 100th opponent?

121
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:11,640
Ryu.

122
00:06:12,060 --> 00:06:16,640
Whoa, congrats on preventing your 100th straight win, Ryu.

123
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:18,480
Why are you here?

124
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:19,940
You can't just show up unannounced!

125
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:21,440
This is my room, though.

126
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,060
Um, by any chance...

127
00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:25,200
Hmm?

128
00:06:25,540 --> 00:06:27,000
Are you...

129
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,400
Are you two dating each other?

130
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:38,840
I knew it.

131
00:06:41,060 --> 00:06:41,980
No way!

132
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:45,640
It's a yes or no question, so you should pick one, Ryu.

133
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:46,900
Uh-huh.

134
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:49,020
Don't confirm something when it's not true!

135
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:52,880
I suppose me and Shizuru are more like brothers than anything else.

136
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:55,540
Hold up! Who's the older brother and who's the younger one?

137
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:57,840
That's your biggest concern about this.

138
00:06:57,840 --> 00:06:58,620
Oh, I see.

139
00:06:58,880 --> 00:06:59,060
Huh?

140
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:02,740
I don't have any siblings, so I'm totally envious.

141
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:04,360
Not you too, Sadako.

142
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:08,280
Laughter.

143
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:14,300
An exuberant place.

144
00:07:16,320 --> 00:07:18,220
Friends who I truly love.

145
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:23,820
Staying by their side.

146
00:07:24,260 --> 00:07:27,000
It really is okay, isn't it?

147
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:34,140
Hey, should we call of Kaze Haya while we're here?

148
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:35,960
K-Call Kaze Haya?

149
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:39,760
Can't let Ryu be the only one allowed to enjoy the harem, right?

150
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:41,600
The what?

151
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:45,080
Well, I imagine it's tough being the lone guy in a room.

152
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:46,740
Ryu, cell phone.

153
00:07:46,740 --> 00:07:48,080
You call him, Sadako.

154
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:48,500
You call him, Sadako.

155
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:52,500
Here.

156
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:54,360
Wait, me?

157
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:54,960
Uh-huh.

158
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:57,000
Are you sure that's okay?

159
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:58,120
Why wouldn't it be?

160
00:07:58,360 --> 00:07:59,880
Come on, just call him already.

161
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:04,260
Kaze Haya's gonna pick up thinking it's Ryu and be super shocked when he hears a girl's voice.

162
00:08:04,260 --> 00:08:06,720
Press the phone button to start calling.

163
00:08:09,940 --> 00:08:11,540
My heart is racing.

164
00:08:12,980 --> 00:08:14,960
There's nothing to be so nervous about.

165
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:17,200
Kaze Haya's definitely gonna be the one to pick up.

166
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:18,720
He is?

167
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:21,060
Now my heart's racing even more.

168
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:24,280
Say, we're having fun.

169
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:24,920
Hurry over.

170
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:27,100
Or Ryu's outnumbered by girls.

171
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:27,800
Save him.

172
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:34,800
Well...

173
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:40,840
I'd like him to be here.

174
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,320
Hmm?

175
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:51,440
A phone call!

176
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:52,660
Who is it, huh, Shota?

177
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:53,460
Tell me!

178
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:55,240
Oh, that's Ryu.

179
00:08:55,980 --> 00:08:56,500
Giddy!

180
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:58,240
I want to talk to him, too!

181
00:08:58,480 --> 00:08:59,260
Chill out.

182
00:08:59,380 --> 00:08:59,880
No!

183
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,040
Hey, come on!

184
00:09:01,140 --> 00:09:01,760
Stop it!

185
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:05,140
Is this Kaze Haya?

186
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:07,100
It's Kuro Numa.

187
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:07,640
Ryu!

188
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:09,060
Can you hear me?

189
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:09,880
I want to talk!

190
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,460
Wait, what do you mean this is?

191
00:09:12,620 --> 00:09:14,020
But isn't this the number for...

192
00:09:14,020 --> 00:09:14,800
How come...

193
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:15,940
What's going on?

194
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:20,360
So, I met Sanada's and...

195
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:21,320
Ryu's house?

196
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:24,140
Iyano Yoshida and I went to get ramen today.

197
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:26,360
So that's why I'm with them all right now.

198
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:26,760
Okay.

199
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:29,240
I...

200
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:31,260
I'm really having a lot of fun.

201
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:33,500
Being with everyone makes things more enjoyable.

202
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:35,820
And if you were here, too,

203
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:38,760
we thought it'd be even more fun than it already is.

204
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:41,580
I'll zip over on my bike.

205
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:46,040
He's on his way!

206
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:46,480
Now!

207
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:47,280
I'll say hi, huh?

208
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:48,100
You were...

209
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:50,200
having that much fun with us?

210
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:52,240
And that's me!

211
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:53,600
Ah!

212
00:09:53,600 --> 00:10:10,400
And that's me!

213
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:15,040
You three have really been in the same class

214
00:10:15,040 --> 00:10:16,340
ever since you were in middle school?

215
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:17,920
For second and third year.

216
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:22,160
Hmm, Ryu and Kaze Haya are...

217
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:24,160
He hasn't changed even a bit.

218
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:26,800
Hmm, for as long as I can remember,

219
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:28,580
he's always looked exactly the same.

220
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:30,640
But I've gotten so much taller.

221
00:10:33,220 --> 00:10:33,740
Whoa!

222
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:38,140
This must be Kaze Haya's middle school photo.

223
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:42,280
So this must be everyone's Kaze Haya, huh?

224
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:43,940
Too baby-faced for me.

225
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:44,680
His hair!

226
00:10:44,940 --> 00:10:46,840
Ah, he was growing it out then.

227
00:10:46,840 --> 00:10:49,320
It was after shaving his head for baseball season.

228
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:52,660
But Ryu's always had a buzz cut, regardless of playing sports.

229
00:10:52,980 --> 00:10:54,020
Cause it's easy.

230
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:55,620
That's the kind of guy he is.

231
00:10:58,620 --> 00:11:00,240
Shota's a great baseball player.

232
00:11:00,820 --> 00:11:02,400
When he didn't join our high school team,

233
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:04,080
Kane was pretty disappointed.

234
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:08,640
A side of Kaze Haya that I was unaware of.

235
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:11,700
I wonder what he was like in middle school.

236
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:15,380
Was he someone who studied earnestly?

237
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:18,420
And got in as much practice as he could?

238
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:22,160
I wish I could have seen him play.

239
00:11:22,860 --> 00:11:23,940
Oh, you probably can.

240
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:26,160
Our field day is coming up fairly soon.

241
00:11:26,460 --> 00:11:28,880
I bet Kaze Haya will join the softball team.

242
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:30,620
Is that true?

243
00:11:30,620 --> 00:11:35,540
I can watch Kaze Haya in the present going forward.

244
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:38,920
Not to mention, I can be in the pictures with everyone.

245
00:11:39,340 --> 00:11:41,700
And be invited to do so many things with them.

246
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:46,320
There's field day, school trips, and a whole lot more.

247
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:48,660
I'm really excited.

248
00:11:49,460 --> 00:11:51,280
I'm excited for everything.

249
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:52,820
You'll have fun.

250
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:53,680
I know it.

251
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:55,920
And you'll eat tons of good food, too.

252
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:58,340
Now that I have friends,

253
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:01,040
I can share the same joys with all of them.

254
00:12:02,020 --> 00:12:04,340
Oh, this girl is...

255
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:04,620
Huh?

256
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:06,040
That's Kurumi.

257
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:07,060
How do you know her?

258
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:09,020
She helped me pick up some handouts

259
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:10,480
that I dropped in the hallway once.

260
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:13,900
What's that face you're making, Chizu?

261
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:15,540
Uh, it's nothing.

262
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,060
Looks like the kind to be popular with the guys.

263
00:12:18,300 --> 00:12:19,140
Yep, that's her.

264
00:12:20,340 --> 00:12:21,200
Ryo, look.

265
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:22,220
What's your verdict?

266
00:12:24,220 --> 00:12:25,340
She's not my type.

267
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:28,420
Whoa, I didn't think you actually had a type.

268
00:12:28,780 --> 00:12:30,500
Okay, then what about this one here?

269
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:36,420
I like her fine.

270
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:40,540
Well, I like you fine also, Sanada.

271
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:45,140
And what about the two of us?

272
00:12:46,520 --> 00:12:48,080
I... I love you.

273
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:49,860
